    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A kingdom of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#caucasus">Caucasus</a> between the Kura river and the Caspian, roughly the north and centre of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</li><li>A client first of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> and then of Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#persia">Persia</a>, it guarded the Caspian passes against raiders from the steppe.</li><li>It adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#christianity">Christianity</a> in the 4th century and had its own church and alphabet, whose texts survive in Sinai palimpsests.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A Roman legion left a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a> inscription at Gobustan near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#baku">Baku</a> under the emperor Domitian, the easternmost Latin inscription known.</p></aside>
    </section>

